  "worked_solution": "Previously we found that the line $\\overset{\u2194}{AB}$ has the equation\n\n$$\ny=-3x+7.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. \n\n* Since the line is *dashed*, we will use a *strict* inequality. \n\n* Since the shaded region is *below* the line, the inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line.\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<-3x+7.\n$$",
